{
    "Description": {
        "Id": "starsystemdef_Farceland",
        "Name": "Farceland",
        "Details": "Farceland was named for being something of a joke, at least at first, as it was one of the first worlds established by pirates where such outlaws are in charge of and manage the planet, yet have a puppet-type of pretend local government that they control, which pretends to fight them for being outlaws, yet has instructions to lose against the outlaws, as something of a game that on top of all things isn't exactly a secret.  Anyways, while the place is a rough neighborhood and high-crime planet, there is a substantial population here, including families and children who go to school, and so on, and a massive amount of trade and merchandise that flows in and out and around the whole planet, including special inventories from other factions, along with thriving industries and businesses in this jungle world that is roughly Earth-sized.  Farceland is also an agricultural center, with many jungle farms, and it produces food for the pirates who run it and have their own private set of worlds in this region of space.  Understand that if you accept any work contracts here, you are working for pirates and also fighting against pirates who are overall the same.  Its complicated and it is weird, but it's best to simply take the money and keep your mouth shut and not ask questions, and put on a show for pirates who have their entertainment out of it.  With any work contract, there are pirates betting real money on you as well as against you, more or less behind the scenes.",
